Z||000000||varnster||09-27-2001||04:05 PM||||It has 60,000 miles on it, he want $450 for<BR>it and will install for $350, He says it runs very smooth and in very good condition.<BR>I dont know much about pricing these things<BR>out. what do YOU think? it is for an 87gt. ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Hank is Here||09-27-2001||04:07 PM||||That is an Al. headed engine, you have an iron headed engine.  It is a bolt in but needs computer work.  Probably not worth it.  Keep looking for a Camaro 3.4||||reg||1
Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||09-27-2001||04:09 PM||||Great Only if he'll swap your 2.8 Heads/Intake before installing it. Then it'll fit the harness and no computer change needed.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Hank is Here||09-27-2001||04:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B>Great Only if he'll swap your 2.8 Heads/Intake before installing it. Then it'll fit the harness and no computer change needed.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Mint, <BR>isn't there a compression difference in the pistons too? Thought if you used an AL motor and iron head you would have way low compression ratio. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Voytek||09-27-2001||04:42 PM||||- Yes, it's a good price for the engine AND the install.<BR>- Yes, it'll fit just fine.<P>Now, keep in mind that you'll need the computer swapped and a new location for the coil pack (it would be agains the firewall - too tight) - it does have a coil pack and not a distributor, right?<P>You CAN swap the heads but don't have to.  It all depends on what look you want.  If you want the Fiero red intake you'll need to swap the heads - the intakes do not interchange.  If you don't mind the silver top with the 3.1 written on it, it'll fit just fine.<P>I've also heard the exhaust manifolds don't swap over.  I've checked it out physically - yes, they do fit.<P>All in all, I think it's a really good engine.  I've had my 2.8 redone into a 3.1 and now I'm wishing I had gone with the aluminum head 3.1 - it has a nice power advantage over the stock 2.8.  I've seen it in a couple of Fieros and they were both quite fast.<P>Make sure your mechanic knows the details of the swap (computer, harness, coil pack and maybe misc.).<P>I'd really say go for it.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||varnster||09-27-2001||05:22 PM||||Not sure about the coil pack, I called and left a message. By swapping the heads and intake from a 2.8 to the 3.1 will this negate<BR>any performance gained by using the 3.1? I<BR>want to keep it factory looking, so i do want<BR>to use the 2.8 stuff. Am I just pissing in the wind! keep in mind I have an auto trany,<BR>will this give me {bluntly} more SPEED!||||reg||1
